From f8e1679169631c50d080c4fb1f0f83fcae2efc47 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 15:24:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] skin.estuary: the Dolby Vision page says the video scaling
 method is not used

A user set the video scaling method to nearest neighbour in every video,
believing that it chose how the enhancement layer of profile 7 is scaled up.
It does not. A picture that the Dolby Vision engine draws, natively or rebuilt
as HDR10, is drawn by the bridge before Kodi's renderer would apply the
setting (CLinuxRendererGLES::Render() returns after RenderDVBridge() or
RenderDVConversion(), before UpdateVideoFilter()): the enhancement layer is
resampled as ETSI GS CCM 001 says, and the picture is scaled with libplacebo's
defaults (Lanczos up, Hermite down). Only the fidelity step-down, where the GPU
cannot keep up, makes some of those filters bilinear. The setting applies to
the ordinary output: HDR10, HLG, SDR, and Dolby Vision shown by its base layer.

The page says so where the engine draws: "Video scaling method: not used for
Dolby Vision", the setting as the video settings name it (#16300).

With native output the right list of that page has eight rows, and its panel
had room for seven: the eighth fell 38 pixels below it. With this row the left
list has eight as well. The page has a panel of its own, a row taller.
